The FM engine in src/fm6/ is a TypeScript port of fm6_core.c from Felucca
(https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca, GPL-3.0-only, Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita,
Hügelton Instruments), which is itself an integer C port of msfa, the 6-operator FM core of Dexed:
  Copyright 2012 Google Inc., Copyright 2016-2025 Pascal Gauthier, licensed under Apache-2.0
  (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
Its lookup tables follow Felucca's tools/gen_tables.py and Felucca-Engines (MIT).

tests/fm6-gold.txt holds reference output produced by Felucca's fm6_core.c.

src/fm6/bank.ts: the WebSynth factory voices are original works of this project (GPL-3.0-only). They are written as
readable operator settings and were not copied from any instrument ROM.
src/fm6/factory.ts: the INIT voice and Felucca's 8 factory voices (GPL-3.0-only, Leo Kuroshita / Hügelton Instruments).

src/engines/: TypeScript ports of Felucca-Engines (https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca-Engines, MIT, Copyright (C) 2026
Leo Kuroshita, Hügelton Instruments): the shared DSP helpers and tables (dsp.c, gen_engine_tables.py), the ANALOG
engine and its host contract. tests/engines-golden.txt is that project's reference output (tests/golden.txt).

src/fx/: TypeScript ports of the effects of Felucca's fx.c (GPL-3.0-only): DIST, chorus, tempo delay, the ROOM,
SPRING and HALL reverbs and the master limiter. tests/fx-gold.txt is reference output of that code.
src/drum/: TypeScript ports of Felucca's drum_voice.c and the lane/kit logic of eng_drum.c (GPL-3.0-only).
tests/drum-gold.txt is reference output of drum_voice.c.

src/engines/formant.ts, src/engines/phys.ts: TypeScript ports of Felucca's eng_formant.c (VOICE, after Klatt 1980 and klattsch design
notes), eng_phys.c, phys_dsp.c and phys_symp.c (PHYS: DaisySP by Electrosmith / Emilie Gillet, MIT; Rings by Emilie Gillet, MIT; fixed-point ports
by Leo Kuroshita, GPL-3.0-only). tests/voice-gold.txt and tests/phys-gold.txt are reference output of that C code.

src/sampler/: TypeScript ports of Felucca's eng_sample.c, eng_grain.c and eng_slice.c (GPL-3.0-only) and their sample data
(tools/gen_samples.py output). The piano, flute and tenor sax sets are IMA ADPCM encodings of CC0 1.0 recordings by
Versilian Studios (Sam Gossner): VSCO-2 Community Edition (https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE) and VCSL
(https://github.com/sgossner/VCSL). The drum break of SLICE is built from Felucca's generated drums (the Hügelton Sample
Pack, CC0 1.0). tests/sample-gold.txt, grain-gold.txt and slice-gold.txt are reference output of the C code.
